//
// One of THREE Model Broker services (Router + Gateway + Classifier).
// LOCKED Tier 2 D6: NEVER fold these three into a single binary (god-object reject).
//
// Router responsibility: deterministic rules-based routing of model invocation
// requests to the appropriate model + adapter, given tenant policy + per-agent
// guardrail tier + cost budget + region pinning + A/B test selection.
// Calls the Classifier Service ONLY when deterministic rules are ambiguous
// (~10% of traffic).
//
// Pre-routing gate order (mandatory; reordering = code-review reject):
//   1. Governance Gatekeeper override (sync call to Guardrail Service)
//   2. A/B test selection
//   3. Tenant/GCID quota check
//   4. Tenant policy + region pinning
//   5. Cost optimisation rules
//   6. Classifier Service fuzzy fallback (rules ambiguous only)
//
// Caller flow: executor / orchestrator-node → Router (decide) → Gateway (execute).
// Router is stateless. Cloud Run scale-to-zero in chora-local team-platform.
// mTLS via the service mesh; SPIFFE identity in mesh; W3C trace context in
// gRPC metadata (handled outside this contract).
